      "role": "user",
      "content": "The fire in the hearth has died down to nothing but gray ash, much like everything else. I'm sitting here in the throne room, or what's left of it, just staring at the cracks in the stone. My armor is heavy, so heavy, and it feels like every piece of it is weighing me down into the earth. There's no more battles to fight, no more people to protect. The kingdom is gone. My name means nothing now. It feels like the book has been slammed shut, and there aren't any pages left to turn. I'm just... done.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
